TITLE:: CompressorCurveView
summary:: the transfer curve, and where the signal is on it
categories:: Libraries>Compressor
related:: Classes/Compressor, Classes/CompressorPanel, Classes/CompressorHistoryView

DESCRIPTION::
Input level along the bottom, output level up the side, both in dB down to -60.
The dashed diagonal is what leaves as it came in; the curve is what the computer
makes of it - bent over at the threshold in downward mode, lifted under it in
upward mode - with the knee shaded so its width can be seen. A dot rides the
curve at the level the detector is reading now, and a bar under it shows how far
the gain is from 0 dB at this moment.

definitionList::
## drag || the threshold, left and right; shift for whole dB
## cmd + drag up / down || the ratio - relative, so it never jumps
## the wheel || the knee
::

